  "type": "problem",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<div><p>Arrange every card in hand into groups containing exactly groupSize cards. Within each group the values must be consecutive integers, with each card used once. Return whether such a complete arrangement exists. Duplicate values represent distinct cards, so they may belong to different groups.</p><p>An empty hand can be split into zero groups, and is therefore valid for every positive groupSize.</p><p><strong>Example 1</strong></p><pre>Input: hand = [1,2,3,6,2,3,4,7,8], groupSize = 3\nOutput: true</pre><p>Explanation: Use groups [1,2,3], [2,3,4], and [6,7,8].</p><p><strong>Example 2</strong></p><pre>Input: hand = [1,2,3,4,5], groupSize = 4\nOutput: false</pre><p>Explanation: Five cards cannot fill groups of four without leftovers.</p><p><strong>Example 3</strong></p><pre>Input: hand = [4,4,4], groupSize = 1\nOutput: true</pre><p>Explanation: With size one, each of the three cards forms its own group.</p><p><strong>Constraints</strong></p><ul><li>0 ≤ hand.length ≤ 10,000.</li><li>1 ≤ groupSize ≤ 10,000.</li><li>0 ≤ hand[i] ≤ 1,000,000,000.</li></ul></div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def isNStraightHand(self, hand: List[int], groupSize: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Return the requested result.\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "var isNStraightHand = function(hand, groupSize) {\n    // your code here\n};\n"
  },
